I now have a complete picture. Here is my thorough report.

## Overview

This is a Spring/OfficeFloor PetClinic variant. The "region-and-hash identity" logic lives almost entirely in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`. Important: there are **three inconsistent states** of the identity design in the repo — the live implementation, a stale OpenAPI/Mapper spec, and an acceptance test describing a *not-yet-implemented* unified `memberId`. I flag these below.

---

## 1. customerCode — computation and format

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java` (lines 18-38). Sets `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>`, i.e. `Locality.of(owner) + "-" + hash8(telephone + lastName)`. `hash8` (lines 24-37) takes SHA-256 of the UTF-8 bytes of the seed and formats the **first 4 bytes as 8 UPPER-case hex chars** (`%02X`).

```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
    owner.setCustomerCode(Locality.of(owner) + "-" + hash8(owner.getTelephone() + owner.getLastName()));
}
private static String hash8(String seed) {
    byte[] digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256").digest(seed.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
    StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder(8);
    for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) { sb.append(String.format("%02X", digest[i])); }
    return sb.toString();
}
```

Wired into the create flow in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` (lines 43-46, `assignCustomerCode`), running after all validation and before `deduplicateCustomerCode` (lines 48-51).

Storage field: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` lines 52-53 (`@Column(name = "customer_code") private String customerCode;`), getter/setter lines 91-97.

**Discrepancy:** the OpenAPI spec `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` lines 2130-2134 documents `customerCode` as format `'<LAST3>-<NNNN>'`, example `SMI-0007` — this does **not** match the actual `<REGION>-<HASH8>` implementation. The spec doc is stale.

## 2. membershipNumber — computation and format

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/MembershipNumber.java` (lines 11-22). Format `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where YY = last two digits of the fiscal year of `registrationDate`. Returns `null` if customerCode or registrationDate absent.

```java
public static String of(Owner owner) {
    if (owner.getCustomerCode() == null || owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) return null;
    return String.format("%s-M%02d", owner.getCustomerCode(), FiscalYear.of(owner.getRegistrationDate()) % 100);
}
```

Documented in openapi.yml lines 2136-2141 (example `SMI-0007-M26`).

## 3. checkDigit — Luhn

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CheckDigit.java` (lines 8-36). Luhn over the digits of `customerCode`, doubling from the rightmost digit, non-digits skipped; returns `null` when code absent.

```java
public static Integer of(String customerCode) {
    if (customerCode == null) return null;
    int sum = 0; boolean dbl = true;
    for (int i = customerCode.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        char c = customerCode.charAt(i);
        if (c < '0' || c > '9') continue;
        int d = c - '0';
        if (dbl) { d *= 2; if (d > 9) d -= 9; }
        sum += d; dbl = !dbl;
    }
    return (10 - (sum % 10)) % 10;
}
```

A duplicate Luhn implementation exists in the test base: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` `luhn(String s)` starting line 302. Documented in openapi.yml lines 2142-2149.

## 4. HASH8 — SHA-256 region-and-hash identity

The HASH8 itself is computed in `AssignOwnerCustomerCode.hash8` (see item 1): SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`, first 4 bytes → 8 UPPER-case hex chars.

Note the seed is the **raw** `owner.getTelephone() + owner.getLastName()` — despite the class Javadoc (lines 10-16) saying "normalised telephone." No separate normalization is applied here (telephone is already validated E.164 by the `@Pattern` on `Owner.telephone`, Owner.java lines 47-50).

A parallel full-length SHA-256 identity used for *duplicate detection* (not the customerCode) lives in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/IdentityKey.java` (lines 16-38): SHA-256 hex over `telephone + "|" + lowercased email + "|" + Soundex(lastName)`, full 64-char lower-case hex. Used by `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureOwnerIdentityUnique.java` (lines 13-25).

Test helper replicating HASH8: `AcceptanceBase.shaHex(String s, int n)` (line 297) returns first `n` UPPER-case hex chars of `sha256hex` (line 282).

## 5. Fiscal year (FY)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/FiscalYear.java` (lines 14-27). FY starts 1 July (July-Dec → next calendar year). `of(LocalDate)` returns the int FY; `label(Owner)` returns `FY<YY>` (or null).

```java
public static int of(LocalDate date) {
    return date.getMonthValue() >= Month.JULY.getValue() ? date.getYear() + 1 : date.getYear();
}
public static String label(Owner owner) {
    LocalDate registration = owner.getRegistrationDate();
    return registration == null ? null : String.format("FY%02d", of(registration) % 100);
}
```

Also consumed by `MembershipNumber` (item 2) and by tenure scoring in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/MembershipLevel.java` (`hasTenure`, lines 39-43). Documented in openapi.yml lines 2246-2251 (example `FY26`).

## 6. Collision handling

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/DeduplicateOwnerCustomerCode.java` (lines 15-29). If the computed customerCode is already held by another owner, appends `-<n>` with the smallest `n >= 2` that is unique.

```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    Set<String> taken = new HashSet<>();
    for (Owner other : ownerRepository.findAll()) { taken.add(other.getCustomerCode()); }
    String base = owner.getCustomerCode();
    String code = base;
    for (int n = 2; taken.contains(code); n++) { code = base + "-" + n; }
    owner.setCustomerCode(code);
}
```

Runs right after `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` (owners.POST.yml lines 48-51). Note: appended `-<n>` digits will feed into the Luhn `checkDigit`.

## 7. The audit record

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RespondWithOwnerCreated.java` (lines 16-40). Emits TWO audit lines to a dedicated SLF4J logger named `"AUDIT"`:
- Human-readable (lines 33-34): `owner created id=... customerCode=... registrationDate=... membershipLevel=... membershipNumber=...`
- JSON with a per-process `AtomicInteger SEQ` (line 18, incremented line 37): `{"seq":..,"ownerId":..,"customerCode":"..","membershipLevel":..,"event":"OWNER_CREATED"}`

Test-side capture of that logger: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` (whole file, class lines 25-79) — attaches a Logback `ListAppender` to the `"AUDIT"` logger and exposes `messages()`, `anyContains(...)`, `anyAtLevel(...)`, `count()`.

## 8. The owner segment

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerSegment.java` (lines 12-24). Format `<TIER>_<AREA>`: TIER = `PREMIUM` when membershipLevel >= 3 else `STANDARD`; AREA = `METRO` when `Locality.of(owner)` is in `{NSW, VIC, QLD}` (constant `KNOWN_REGIONS`, line 14) else `REGIONAL`.

```java
public static String of(int membershipLevel, Owner owner) {
    String tier = membershipLevel >= 3 ? "PREMIUM" : "STANDARD";
    String area = KNOWN_REGIONS.contains(Locality.of(owner)) ? "METRO" : "REGIONAL";
    return tier + "_" + area;
}
```

Populated onto the DTO in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RespondWithOwner.java` line 21. Documented openapi.yml lines 2200-2205.

Region derivation used by segment/customerCode: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/Locality.java` (lines 13-42) — postcode ranges (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099) preferred, else city→region table, else `UNKNOWN`. Region range validation also in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureOwnerPostcodeWithinRegion.java` (lines 14-30).

## 9. DTO/entity fields and mapping

- Entity: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — `customerCode` (lines 52-53, 91-97), `registrationDate` (lines 99-130). No stored membershipNumber/checkDigit/fiscalYear/ownerSegment — these are **derived at mapping time**.
- Mapper: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` `toOwnerDto` (lines 21-34). Relevant `@Mapping` expressions: `membershipNumber` → `MembershipNumber.of(owner)` (line 27), `fiscalYear` → `FiscalYear.label(owner)` (line 28), `checkDigit` → `CheckDigit.of(owner.getCustomerCode())` (line 29), `identityKey` → `IdentityKey.of(owner)` (line 26), `locality` → `Locality.of(owner)` (line 30). (`ownerSegment` is set imperatively in `RespondWithOwner`, not via the mapper.)
- DTO schema (OwnerDto is generated from OpenAPI): `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` — `customerCode` 2130-2135, `membershipNumber` 2136-2141, `checkDigit` 2142-2150, `identityKey` 2157-2162, `locality` 2194-2199, `ownerSegment` 2200-2205, `fiscalYear` 2246-2251 (plus namesakeCount/membershipPoints/membershipLevel 2163-2187).

### Tests referencing these

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` (whole file, 21 lines). **This test describes a target design that is NOT implemented yet.** Its header comment (lines 7-9) and `coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId` (lines 12-20) assert that `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` are **unified into a single `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`**, that `memberId` starts with the region (`NSW`), contains `shaHex(telephone+lastName, 8)`, and that the old `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` fields are **removed**. The current implementation still exposes both old fields and has no `memberId`, so this test would currently fail — a likely intended refactor target.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — helpers: `sha256hex` (282), `shaHex` (297, the HASH8 replica), `luhn` (302), `region`/`CITY_REGION`/`REGION_POSTCODES`/`REGION_TIMEZONE` (227-256), `knownOwner`/`validPostcode` (252-265), `toBusinessDay`/`HOLIDAYS` (239-274).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` — audit assertion harness (item 7).

### Key inconsistencies to be aware of
1. **customerCode format**: implementation `<REGION>-<HASH8>` vs openapi.yml doc `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (SMI-0007). Doc is stale.
2. **identityKey format**: openapi.yml lines 2157-2162 documents it as `<normalizedTelephone>|<email>|<householdId>`, but `IdentityKey.java` actually produces a 64-char SHA-256 hex over `telephone|email|Soundex(lastName)`. Doc is stale.
3. **Unified memberId**: only `AcceptanceTest.java` references `memberId`/`<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`; no production code computes it. This is a pending/target design not yet built.

